From e29b9fdf98b4b4357d5d8e215830416241e2f991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] L1 threads: raise RecursionError before entering the
 scheduler near the recursion limit (a RecursionError inside it wedged every
 thread: easypy suite, exploration seeds); harness: thread-heavy suites first

The depth check runs only on slow paths (contended acquire, a possible switch,
sleep, I/O, join, start), so an uncontended lock costs the same as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
